Z||000000||fiero_nightmare||10-29-2001||10:23 AM||||i am making a home made side scoop out of fiberglass for my fiero and i am almost done. the problem i am having is i made it kind of small so there is not much room for bolts like i originally planned. so i have to find a way to bond the fiberglass scoop to the plastic.  <P>will fiberglass stick to plastic good if i take off all of the paint? or does anyone know what else will work?<P><BR>i am going to get another lower 1/4 panel so i don't ruin my factory panel.<P>------------------<BR>my 85 GT pics <P>http://communities.msn.com/russcars/85fierogt.msnw||||reg||5
Z||000001||skitime||10-29-2001||11:09 AM||||I use a two part epoxy designed to repair urethane body panels.  It is expensive but works great and is sandable. You can purchase at any automotive finishing supplier. It will hold well to both materials.  My car should be the poster child for this stuff. I used it in many modifications.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
